-- A TYPICALLY default that is an expression (W7) meeting a multi-clause group
-- (several DECIDE clauses of one rule) and CONSIDER. Every answer below was
-- worked out by hand; typically-multi-clause.l4 has the literal-default cases.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

DECLARE Paint
  HAS colour IS A Colour TYPICALLY Red
      coats  IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`standard rate` MEANS 3

-- (a) A multi-clause group whose GIVEN carries defaults: a literal and an
-- expression (W7). A named call leaves both out.
GIVEN c    IS A Colour
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      mult IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (`standard rate` TIMES 2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `price of` Red   rate mult IS rate TIMES 10
DECIDE `price of` Green rate mult IS rate TIMES mult
DECIDE `price of` Blue  rate mult IS 0

#EVAL `price of` WITH c IS Red
#EVAL `price of` WITH c IS Green
#EVAL `price of` WITH c IS Green, rate IS 5
#EVAL `price of` WITH c IS Blue

-- (b) A default reached inside a CONSIDER branch the drafter wrote.
GIVEN x IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
`via consider` MEANS
  CONSIDER x
  WHEN Red   THEN `price of` WITH c IS Green
  WHEN Green THEN (Paint WITH coats IS 1)'s coats PLUS 100
  OTHERWISE 0

#EVAL `via consider` Red
#EVAL `via consider` Green
#EVAL `via consider` Blue

-- (c) A named site and a construction inside the clauses of a group.
GIVEN k IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `grouped` Red   IS `price of` WITH c IS Green
DECIDE `grouped` Green IS
  CONSIDER (Paint WITH coats IS 2)'s colour
  WHEN Red THEN 7
  OTHERWISE 8
DECIDE `grouped` Blue  IS `price of` WITH c IS Red, rate IS 1

#EVAL `grouped` Red
#EVAL `grouped` Green
#EVAL `grouped` Blue

-- (d) A group with no GIVEN for its columns, one clause matching anything
-- first, then an unreachable clause that takes a default.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `no given` Red   IS `price of` WITH c IS Green
DECIDE `no given` other IS 1
DECIDE `no given` Blue  IS `price of` WITH c IS Red

#EVAL `no given` Red
#EVAL `no given` Blue

-- (e) A one-clause group with a default; it misses NOTHING.
GIVEN m  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      r2 IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 4
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `one clause` (JUST x) r2 IS x PLUS r2

#EVAL `one clause` WITH m IS JUST 1
